      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand about hip-width with the bar on the floor close to your shins and take a self-selected overhand clean grip.",
        "movement": "Keep the bar close through the first pull and rebend, extend the hips, knees, and ankles rapidly and shrug, then bend the elbows to pull under and receive the bar across the front shoulders in a full squat.",
        "endpoint": "Stand fully with your feet on one line and become still; dip, drive the bar upward, split one foot forward and the other back, and receive it overhead with both elbows straight.",
        "returnPhase": "Recover until both feet are on one line under the locked-out bar, become still, then lower the bar to the floor before the next repetition.",
        "controlledJoints": "Control hip, knee, and ankle flexion in the clean catch and knee flexion in the split receive; complete the clean recovery before beginning the jerk.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Brace the trunk, keep a secure two-hand grip, and use no external support.",
